WEBVTT

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:12.130
What's with you, guys?

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:16.470
How foolish!

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:17.550
Are you really

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:20.930
the String Masters
in the predictions of the future?

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:23.310
Are you the ones responsible
for the future of humanity?

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.150
-But I--
-I can't believe

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:30.360
you are worth my friends and family
risking their lives

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:32.990
-to protect you.
-What?

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:35.070
How dare you question our worth?

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.370
You dragged us into this,
so you have no right to say that.

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:40.540
But you're involved in this now,

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:44.080
-so--
-Nobody told me I'd have to kill people!

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:46.040
-What?
-Kill people?

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:47.000
I heard it all!

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.250
Milo tricked us!

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:52.010
She's using us as tools to kill people!

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:53.630
Calm down, Marimari.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.220
Those giant beasts

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:57.430
that we killed...

00:00:57.510 --> 00:00:59.180
-Those were humans!
-What?

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:00.260
How can that be?

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.140
What's this all about, Milo?

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:05.520
The beasts inside
the Revisions' machines are

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:08.900
humans.

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:47.200
NO TRESPASSING

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:49.500
<i>The Civilian beasts are humans?</i>

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:51.880
What do you mean by that?

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:57.670
After the world was overrun
by the RV virus,

00:02:58.380 --> 00:02:59.800
humanity was split into two groups.

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:02.300
Humans that were immune
and those who weren't.

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:05.350
Later, those became AHRV
and the Revisions.

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:09.770
The nations combined forces
to develop a vaccine,

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:12.600
but the virus mutated
with every generation,

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:14.060
making extermination impossible.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:15.730
Then what?

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:18.320
Infected people suffered
a metabolic disorder

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:22.950
that radically swelled their extremities,
then their cells died, leading to death.

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:27.160
<i>Swollen extremities?
I can't believe that's all that is.</i>

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:29.160
<i>Those things aren't even living beings.</i>

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:31.790
<i>I told you,
humans were split into two groups.</i>

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:35.090
<i>How the heck can they support
their enormous bodies?</i>

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:36.340
<i>I mean, their bones...</i>

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.090
<i>So you've realized it now.</i>

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:41.930
<i>They used machines
to reinforce their bodies.</i>

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:44.090
Is that what those Civilians are?

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:45.100
That's right.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:48.970
What about their brains?
Hasn't the disease destroyed them too?

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:52.390
They're constantly replaced
with normal cells, so that doesn't happen.

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:53.600
Normal cells?

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:55.310
That means cells of other people.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:04:00.530
To obtain normal cells, they attacked
people resistant to the disease

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:02.110
without hesitation.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.030
So, everyone was killed?

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:06.240
<i>Some people died in the wars,</i>

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:10.500
<i>but the majority people
were killed for extracting their cells.</i>

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:14.040
They say that
the Shibuya Operation Revisions is

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:17.340
to prevent the pandemic,
but I don't believe them.

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:21.470
They just want to replenish
their dwindling supply of normal cells.

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:24.720
We're just materials they plan to use
to help them survive?

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:27.220
Milo, do the Civilians have intelligence?

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.180
<i>No, they have almost no intelligence.</i>

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:32.140
<i>The cells they collect are
just enough to keep them barely alive.</i>

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:34.690
Then they're not really humans, right?

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:38.730
You're going to determine if they're human
by the intelligence they have?

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:40.400
That's not what I meant.

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:41.610
Then what did you mean?

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:43.240
You self-righteous--

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:44.610
Why?

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:46.570
Why didn't you tell us?

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:48.530
I've told Mr. Kuroiwa and the others.

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:50.450
As for you,

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:54.250
it was AHRV's decision in consideration
of the mental stress it would put on you.

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:56.920
AHRV...

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:02.260
You follow every order of AHRV,
but don't you have a mind of your own?

00:05:02.590 --> 00:05:03.800
What do you think, Milo?

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:05.680
That's what we want to know!

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:07.550
Hold on. Milo has no choice but--

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.010
I can't do this anymore!

00:05:11.140 --> 00:05:13.600
Marimari, we're doing this
to protect everyone.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:16.310
GIRLS

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:20.190
Right, everyone?
We have to do this, you know.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:22.980
-Are you nuts?
-Now, now. Let's not fight.

00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:25.280
We're involved in this now.

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:26.740
That's right.

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:29.620
Since Milo helped us
during the kidnapping,

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:31.740
we've already been involved.

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:34.040
That was our destiny.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:36.790
That was our destiny? Don't make me laugh!

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:39.880
We're just victims who happened to be
in the same place!

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:41.670
But we were friends.

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:42.880
-We're pals.
-Listen!

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:45.420
Each of us had our own dreams!

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:50.390
We were each working hard for our future
and had loving families with us.

00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:52.010
Our future

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:54.770
was completely wiped out!

00:05:56.350 --> 00:05:58.690
You're a lazy-ass NEET! You're a--

00:05:58.770 --> 00:05:59.730
Gai!

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:01.570
Don't say another word!

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:04.650
Wait! Gai!

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:09.610
Gai, Lu.

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:12.830
Keisaku, you understand, don't you?

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:14.080
Well...

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:17.580
Actually, I don't know what to think.

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:20.040
Say, Milo.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:24.670
My mom and the people
who were abducted are still okay, right?

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:25.800
Most likely.

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:27.090
The people on that list

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:29.680
are probably important to them.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:31.640
Most likely, huh?

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:34.760
Keisaku, I swear I'll save your--

00:06:34.890 --> 00:06:37.730
It's okay. It doesn't bother me.

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:39.520
Milo, I'm going to get some sleep.

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:43.110
You'll think over
what Gai and the others said, right?

00:06:43.690 --> 00:06:44.610
Okay, good night.

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:46.570
BOYS

00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:49.320
Your future was wiped out, huh?

00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:51.490
I'll admit, Gai is right.

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:54.950
You guys and I have

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:57.120
<i>very different lives.</i>

00:06:59.290 --> 00:07:01.210
<i>Get away from enemy point six!</i>

00:07:01.290 --> 00:07:02.170
<i>Roger!</i>

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:03.790
<i>Milo?</i>

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:06.760
<i>Don't worry. You should go
to evacuation area three too.</i>

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:08.760
<i>-No, I'll fight alongside you.</i>
-Sis!

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:10.130
<i>Milo. You're all right.</i>

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:11.550
Come to me!

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:12.510
<i>Stay strong!</i>

00:07:12.590 --> 00:07:14.850
<i>You're one of
the few Balancer candidates, you know.</i>

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:16.100
<i>I swear we'll protect you.</i>

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:17.720
<i>The final defense line is down!</i>

00:07:17.810 --> 00:07:19.140
Sis!

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:22.150
<i>We'll stop them here!
Prepare yourselves for the end!</i>

00:07:22.850 --> 00:07:24.480
<i>Milo, live.</i>

00:07:24.650 --> 00:07:26.980
<i>And complete the mission
you've been assigned.</i>

00:07:27.690 --> 00:07:28.740
No!

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:30.320
No!

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:43.790
Sis.

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.300
<i>Gai, you're still thinking about it?</i>

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:51.300
Yes.

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:54.510
This situation we're in is unbelievable,
don't you think?

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:56.010
Daisuke believes it's real.

00:07:56.140 --> 00:07:57.260
This whole thing is crazy.

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:02.020
Don't you think you've been taking
Daisuke's side an awful lot lately?

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:03.270
What's that all about?

00:08:03.690 --> 00:08:05.690
I'm just giving my own opinion.

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:07.730
You know, I kind of wonder.

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:09.440
I mean,

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:11.900
it seems like things ended up
just like Daisuke said.

00:08:12.110 --> 00:08:13.740
Are you saying this was destiny?

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:15.070
That's not what I mean, but...

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:17.660
He has an overactive imagination.

00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:20.540
We need to face reality.

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:23.000
Yes, that's right.

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:24.080
Damn.

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:26.630
I wasn't really myself yesterday either.

00:08:27.130 --> 00:08:29.460
I mean, I know the thing

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:31.380
that I have to do.

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:35.970
What?

00:08:36.090 --> 00:08:37.850
You found a returnee who was abducted?

00:08:37.930 --> 00:08:38.930
Yes.

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:42.310
While Keisuke was on patrol in
a String Puppet, he discovered one male.

00:08:42.390 --> 00:08:45.730
It was Daisuke's uncle, Mikio Dojima.

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:47.520
I just picked him up.

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:49.480
He's weak,

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:50.690
<i>but conscious.</i>

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:52.650
Did he find anyone else?

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:55.030
<i>Keisaku is still searching the area.</i>

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:55.950
Got it.

00:08:56.030 --> 00:08:58.580
<i>Watch the situation and go back
to Disaster Control Headquarters.</i>

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:01.790
Mom!

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:04.290
Where are you?

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:07.080
Mikio!

00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:10.170
Hi.

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:11.300
Mr. Dojima,

00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:14.010
the returnees abducted
by the Revisions are alive

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:16.720
and are being given food and water, right?

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:17.640
Yes.

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:19.680
What was your condition there?

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:22.220
We were isolated in dark rooms.

00:09:22.810 --> 00:09:25.100
But no harm was done to us.

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:26.690
That must mean that...

00:09:27.270 --> 00:09:31.070
That's right. The people they captured
must be their ancestors.

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:35.860
However, a few people were taken away
and never returned.

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:38.240
I made my break then.

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:39.370
They are

00:09:39.570 --> 00:09:43.410
the Civilians' ancestors who died
in war with us or for some other reason.

00:09:43.870 --> 00:09:45.410
There's no need to rescue them now.

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:47.920
Thank goodness, they're all right.

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:49.210
Do you know their location?

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:51.540
I can't tell where exactly.

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:53.340
There were no ruins from our era.

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:57.930
Fortunately, I identified the North Star
and took my chances on escaping South.

00:09:58.010 --> 00:10:01.970
Then they must be in the area
of Shinjuku, Ikebukuro, or Akabane.

00:10:02.060 --> 00:10:03.100
The enemy's base.

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:07.270
Daisuke is here now too,
so we'll leave the rest until later.

00:10:10.770 --> 00:10:13.070
Thank goodness, Mikio.

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:16.400
Daisuke, I heard you've been working hard.

00:10:17.150 --> 00:10:18.320
Mikio.

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:20.700
It looks like things might be
just like you've said.

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:22.200
Take it easy and rest.

00:10:22.280 --> 00:10:23.990
I'll defend Shibuya.

00:10:25.450 --> 00:10:26.870
I'll be counting on you.

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:38.680
<i>So, what about this quantum brain
that's also at the Revisions' base?</i>

00:10:38.760 --> 00:10:42.140
You said Shibuya would return to normal
if it's destroyed, right?

00:10:42.390 --> 00:10:43.260
That's right.

00:10:43.350 --> 00:10:45.310
Then why aren't you attacking it?

00:10:45.640 --> 00:10:48.310
AHRV's military personnel is
around 10,000.

00:10:48.430 --> 00:10:50.100
That's less than the Self-Defense Forces.

00:10:50.770 --> 00:10:53.820
We've been fighting all the Revisions
in the world with that number of people.

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:56.570
The String Puppets were deployed
to Shibuya.

00:10:56.900 --> 00:10:59.280
That means AHRV has concentrated
its military strength here.

00:10:59.900 --> 00:11:02.120
But we can't hold out that long.

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:05.370
<i>Unless we gain some relief,
we won't be able to hold out.</i>

00:11:09.620 --> 00:11:10.500
Marimari.

00:11:10.670 --> 00:11:12.290
I heard your uncle was found.

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:13.590
Yes.

00:11:13.750 --> 00:11:15.040
Thank goodness for that.

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:18.670
So, are you returning
to the String Puppet base?

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:21.180
I have to be on standby,
ready to be deployed at any time.

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:23.300
I guess you're right.

00:11:25.470 --> 00:11:27.640
There's no need for you to pilot
a String Puppet anymore.

00:11:28.310 --> 00:11:30.600
That's my job.
I just need you to back me--

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:31.520
Daisuke,

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:33.440
you seem really energized.

00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:37.190
My uncle encouraged me.

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:38.440
He told me to do my best.

00:11:38.780 --> 00:11:41.150
Sorry if I'm wrong,

00:11:41.780 --> 00:11:45.450
but are you happy that this has happened,
Daisuke?

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:47.330
-What?
-Well, I mean,

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:49.700
you always believed the stuff

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:52.460
that Milo told you
after you were kidnapped, right?

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:54.290
That's right.

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:58.090
That's why everyone thought you were nuts

00:11:58.760 --> 00:12:00.010
ever since middle school.

00:12:01.380 --> 00:12:02.760
Since way back then?

00:12:04.090 --> 00:12:05.890
Was I always worked up over nothing?

00:12:05.970 --> 00:12:06.970
So,

00:12:09.310 --> 00:12:10.850
I thought, maybe

00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:14.060
you don't want to return
to our original time, Daisuke.

00:12:15.770 --> 00:12:16.650
Daisuke?

00:12:16.980 --> 00:12:19.780
No, of course not!

00:12:20.570 --> 00:12:21.490
But...

00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:23.240
"But"?

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:26.280
When Milo showed up
at the school that day,

00:12:26.910 --> 00:12:28.200
all my effort paid off.

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:29.740
That's what I thought.

00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:30.660
I see.

00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:33.460
I guess it's natural you would.

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:35.000
Marimari?

00:12:35.790 --> 00:12:36.630
Sorry.

00:12:36.710 --> 00:12:38.750
I made a promise to Riko and Kaoru.

00:12:41.670 --> 00:12:42.630
What was that all about?

00:12:43.840 --> 00:12:46.640
<i>At that time,
I said it would be by my own strength,</i>

00:12:47.140 --> 00:12:49.350
<i>but Milo gave me the String Puppet.</i>

00:12:49.430 --> 00:12:50.310
STUPID HERO WANNABE

00:12:50.390 --> 00:12:52.480
<i>My destiny to protect everyone</i>

00:12:52.560 --> 00:12:54.730
<i>was supposed to start becoming a reality.</i>

00:12:55.310 --> 00:12:56.230
<i>But...</i>

00:12:58.190 --> 00:13:00.400
It's been a while, Daisuke Dojima.

00:13:02.030 --> 00:13:03.150
Ms. Yumiko.

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:04.950
You look well.

00:13:09.030 --> 00:13:11.080
People do some awful things.

00:13:11.410 --> 00:13:13.330
Did you come here
to give me educational guidance?

00:13:13.750 --> 00:13:15.830
People have many different opinions
here in Shibuya.

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:19.250
Some people don't trust you
and the police.

00:13:19.840 --> 00:13:20.800
Is that so?

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:24.260
Humans show their true colors
when there's a crisis.

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:26.470
It was the same with me.

00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:29.390
I'm ashamed about what I did.

00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:32.560
I should have protected the students,
but fear won out.

00:13:33.100 --> 00:13:34.730
In that situation, you couldn't help it.

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:36.020
But that's exactly why

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:38.650
what you're doing now is amazing.

00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:41.230
Facing those monsters

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:43.650
isn't something anyone can do.

00:13:44.610 --> 00:13:46.780
You're risking your life
for everyone's sake.

00:13:47.280 --> 00:13:50.660
You're one of the chosen ones, right?

00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:52.290
What?

00:13:52.410 --> 00:13:53.910
I'm on your side.

00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:56.870
So, Dojima,

00:13:57.540 --> 00:13:58.620
protect me.

00:14:05.090 --> 00:14:05.970
Okay then.

00:14:06.760 --> 00:14:08.180
See you again.

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:14.140
Hey, Daisuke. Wasn't that...

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:17.440
Forget that. Thank you!

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:18.770
Thank you for finding my uncle!

00:14:19.810 --> 00:14:20.810
Oh, that?

00:14:21.690 --> 00:14:23.110
I feel bad that he's the only one.

00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:24.650
No, don't worry about it.

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:29.820
I guess my bad luck
is Guinness Book of World Records level.

00:14:30.820 --> 00:14:31.820
I have an idea, Keisaku!

00:14:31.910 --> 00:14:33.490
What's with you all of a sudden?

00:14:34.370 --> 00:14:35.410
Leave this to me!

00:14:37.370 --> 00:14:38.830
Are you absolutely sure?

00:14:38.960 --> 00:14:39.790
<i>That's right.</i>

00:14:39.870 --> 00:14:41.920
<i>According to my uncle,
it's somewhere in the North,</i>

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:43.290
<i>around Shinjuku or Ikebukuro.</i>

00:14:44.550 --> 00:14:46.380
Okay, let's try it out.

00:14:46.630 --> 00:14:48.170
If we stay this far apart

00:14:48.510 --> 00:14:51.510
and we head in the same direction with
the Roller deployed, we can't miss it.

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:54.470
<i>Daisuke! Keisaku!
Who gave you permission to do that?</i>

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:56.680
<i>You're not scheduled
to pilot the String Puppet--</i>

00:14:57.520 --> 00:14:58.850
Let's go, Keisaku!

00:14:59.810 --> 00:15:01.520
I'm sorry, Ms. Izumi.

00:15:01.690 --> 00:15:03.520
I just want to save my mom.

00:15:04.570 --> 00:15:06.230
They deployed without permission?

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:07.740
<i>I'm very sorry.</i>

00:15:08.030 --> 00:15:09.990
<i>Based on the info from Mikio Dojima,</i>

00:15:10.110 --> 00:15:12.450
<i>they're going to try and find
the Revisions' base.</i>

00:15:12.570 --> 00:15:14.410
Stop them! Send someone after them!

00:15:14.530 --> 00:15:16.870
<i>But Gai and Lu aren't around now.</i>

00:15:17.450 --> 00:15:18.450
<i>Isn't Temari there?</i>

00:15:18.700 --> 00:15:19.620
Well, you see...

00:15:19.750 --> 00:15:20.830
No way!

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:23.790
I'm not a murderer! I won't pilot it!

00:15:29.380 --> 00:15:30.220
What's wrong?

00:15:30.300 --> 00:15:31.800
<i>Electric field at point-blank...</i>

00:15:31.970 --> 00:15:34.430
<i>Correction. Gravitational field generated.</i>

00:15:39.480 --> 00:15:40.560
What the heck is that?

00:15:43.350 --> 00:15:45.940
<i>Object not found in database.</i>

00:15:46.480 --> 00:15:47.570
<i>Please be careful.</i>

00:15:47.650 --> 00:15:49.110
"Be careful"?

00:15:49.240 --> 00:15:51.030
<i>What is it, Daisuke? The Revisions?</i>

00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:53.490
Yes, but it'll be all right.

00:15:53.610 --> 00:15:55.240
Continue searching, Keisaku.

00:15:55.990 --> 00:15:59.200
I'll defeat you
and prove my value to everyone.

00:15:59.790 --> 00:16:02.370
I'm way better than that Gai!

00:16:02.960 --> 00:16:04.290
Goodness!

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:06.000
What in the world is that?

00:16:06.130 --> 00:16:07.670
This doesn't make any sense.

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:10.050
A spontaneous mutation
from a high-energy object?

00:16:10.170 --> 00:16:13.130
It looks like the artificial quantum brain
has detected something, but...

00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:15.970
Is this the cause?

00:16:16.180 --> 00:16:18.930
That's an AHRV weapon and...
What is that thing?

00:16:19.020 --> 00:16:21.180
It's not one of our comrades?

00:16:21.390 --> 00:16:22.770
Holy crap!

00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:26.730
It does not look like anything
from this era.

00:16:27.320 --> 00:16:28.150
Multiple existences!

00:16:28.400 --> 00:16:29.900
At any rate...

00:16:33.280 --> 00:16:36.370
It might just be a <i>Gespenst</i>.

00:16:36.820 --> 00:16:37.990
A <i>Gespenst</i>?

00:16:38.490 --> 00:16:39.870
So, it's a ghost.

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:46.670
<i>What the heck is with this thing?
Why won't it move?</i>

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:50.710
<i>The object in front of us has been
transmitting data to us.</i>

00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:53.260
<i>-Analyzing.</i>
-Yes. Hurry!

00:16:54.630 --> 00:16:58.140
The two of them deployed alone
to save Keisaku's mom!

00:16:58.220 --> 00:16:59.220
Those idiots!

00:17:01.890 --> 00:17:03.310
<i>Data analysis complete.</i>

00:17:03.890 --> 00:17:05.140
<i>Converting into language.</i>

00:17:06.310 --> 00:17:09.150
<i>"'Believe me. I believe.'</i>

00:17:09.230 --> 00:17:10.650
AI SOUND

00:17:12.110 --> 00:17:15.740
<i>That's right, all you care about</i>

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:18.620
<i>is your own damn destiny.</i>

00:17:18.700 --> 00:17:20.910
<i>You say you'll protect everyone.</i>

00:17:20.990 --> 00:17:24.040
<i>You keep calling yourself a hero
and a champion.</i>

00:17:24.160 --> 00:17:26.790
<i>You just want the people around you
to sing your praises."</i>

00:17:27.790 --> 00:17:30.750
<i>"Daisuke Dojima has no intention
of returning to his original time.</i>

00:17:31.590 --> 00:17:34.300
<i>You were promised that you would be
a hero in this era,</i>

00:17:34.720 --> 00:17:36.880
<i>-so you want to stay here forever.</i>
-That's not true!

00:17:37.890 --> 00:17:39.350
<i>How dare you say we're friends?</i>

00:17:39.430 --> 00:17:40.260
<i>You know</i>

00:17:40.430 --> 00:17:43.270
<i>that deep in your heart,
you wish we were inferior to you."</i>

00:17:43.350 --> 00:17:44.180
That's not true!

00:17:44.270 --> 00:17:48.520
<i>"You never were as good as us
at anything in your original era.</i>

00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:52.820
<i>Daisuke Dojima struggled uselessly
and was all alone.</i>

00:17:52.980 --> 00:17:56.490
-I'll kill you! I'll smash you to bits!
<i>-Daisuke Dojima,</i>

00:17:56.570 --> 00:17:57.820
<i>I will never forgive you.</i>

00:17:59.070 --> 00:18:00.410
<i>Here is your punishment.</i>

00:18:00.580 --> 00:18:03.950
<i>You nonconformist. You weirdo.
You failure."</i>

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:05.580
What's going on?

00:18:06.410 --> 00:18:08.250
<i>Language analysis. "You scoundrel.</i>

00:18:08.540 --> 00:18:12.550
<i>You antisocial person.
You parasite in society.</i>

00:18:12.630 --> 00:18:14.010
<i>You friendless person."</i>

00:18:14.840 --> 00:18:16.170
Holy shit!

00:18:21.140 --> 00:18:23.560
<i>"You can't protect anyone.</i>

00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:26.600
<i>You're not a reliable person
based on your conduct and actions.</i>

00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:29.020
<i>You loser, you dropout.</i>

00:18:31.480 --> 00:18:33.980
<i>Daisuke, I hate your guts."</i>

00:18:34.570 --> 00:18:35.860
Who the hell are you?

00:18:36.150 --> 00:18:38.110
<i>"You ridicule others.</i>

00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:40.660
<i>You mock them as if they were morons.</i>

00:18:41.030 --> 00:18:42.370
<i>But still you want</i>

00:18:42.450 --> 00:18:44.790
<i>to obtain their praise.</i>

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:47.460
<i>You're crude and immature.</i>

00:18:47.750 --> 00:18:49.370
<i>Everything you do is to get noticed.</i>

00:18:49.460 --> 00:18:51.420
<i>-It's all an act."
-Daisuke! Are you okay?</i>

00:18:52.670 --> 00:18:53.670
The String Puppet...

00:18:54.300 --> 00:18:56.710
<i>-Hey! Answer me!</i>
-My String Puppet...

00:18:57.090 --> 00:18:57.920
My power...

00:18:58.010 --> 00:19:00.340
<i>That thing talked to me.</i>

00:19:00.550 --> 00:19:01.390
It talked?

00:19:01.470 --> 00:19:02.800
It has intelligence?

00:19:07.100 --> 00:19:08.100
<i>Hey!</i>

00:19:08.180 --> 00:19:10.770
<i>What the hell happened?
Daisuke, are you all right?</i>

00:19:12.060 --> 00:19:12.980
Yes.

00:19:13.610 --> 00:19:15.020
<i>"You are a coward.</i>

00:19:15.520 --> 00:19:17.490
<i>You are unforgivable."</i>

00:19:17.940 --> 00:19:19.400
<i>That is all, Master.</i>

00:20:50.080 --> 00:20:51.160
Are you okay?

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:52.960
-It's all right now.
-Someone, over here!

00:20:53.040 --> 00:20:54.620
-Thank you.
-It's all right.

00:20:57.000 --> 00:21:00.550
<i>Izumi, why was there a fight
near the border?</i>

00:21:00.630 --> 00:21:01.960
<i>Was it an attack of the Revisions?</i>

00:21:02.050 --> 00:21:05.180
I'm sorry.
I'll find out what's going on now.

00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:08.390
This happened
because I didn't pilot the String Puppet.

00:21:10.060 --> 00:21:13.230
<i>It seems that I've given you
too much leeway until now.</i>

00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:17.440
You deployed a String Puppet without
permission to rescue a friend's family.

00:21:17.810 --> 00:21:21.730
You independently commenced battle with
an unknown object you encountered.

00:21:21.820 --> 00:21:22.820
As a result,

00:21:22.940 --> 00:21:26.700
your machine is destroyed and stray shots
during battle damaged buildings

00:21:26.780 --> 00:21:28.950
and caused numerous casualties.

00:21:29.490 --> 00:21:33.000
This is disappointing. You need to learn
what having responsibility means.

00:21:33.080 --> 00:21:36.040
I was just trying to save the people
that were abducted!

00:21:36.370 --> 00:21:38.170
We're the only ones who can do that!

00:21:38.960 --> 00:21:41.420
And this is the result!

00:21:41.500 --> 00:21:43.420
Since nobody happened to die,

00:21:43.510 --> 00:21:46.800
this is all the punishment you get.
Be grateful!

00:21:49.220 --> 00:21:50.260
So...

00:21:51.010 --> 00:21:52.350
Can the String Puppet be fixed?

00:21:52.560 --> 00:21:55.480
Milo says if we can find the materials,
it can be repaired.

00:21:55.560 --> 00:21:56.730
I see.

00:21:57.650 --> 00:21:58.520
How's Keisaku?

00:21:58.770 --> 00:21:59.770
I'm right next door.

00:22:00.770 --> 00:22:01.820
Oh, I see.

00:22:02.270 --> 00:22:03.480
Sorry. This is my fault.

00:22:03.610 --> 00:22:04.740
It's all right.

00:22:05.070 --> 00:22:07.280
I mean, you tried to save my mom.

00:22:12.160 --> 00:22:14.750
It was just a little mistake.

00:22:15.040 --> 00:22:17.290
Why did Keisuke and I get thrown in here?

00:22:17.750 --> 00:22:19.540
It's like we're criminals!

00:22:19.630 --> 00:22:20.840
Damn them!

00:22:23.590 --> 00:22:24.460
Marimari.

00:22:27.760 --> 00:22:29.340
If only I had piloted it right away...

00:22:30.760 --> 00:22:34.220
If I had known people will get hurt,
I would have done it.

00:22:34.930 --> 00:22:36.600
So tell me to do it, Daisuke.

00:22:36.680 --> 00:22:39.440
Tell me to pilot the String Puppet.

00:22:40.190 --> 00:22:41.520
If you tell me to...

00:22:43.110 --> 00:22:44.480
then I'll...

00:22:45.820 --> 00:22:46.650
I'll...

00:22:50.030 --> 00:22:52.030
Subtitle translation by Brian Athey
